        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### Helical Capsids"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#013",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Capsomers (usually single protein type) arrange around the nucleic acid in a helix.\nThe capsid diameter is determined by the capsomer and the helix parameters; the length\nis determined by the genome length."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#014",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  TOBACCO MOSAIC VIRUS (TMV) — the paradigm:\n  ───────────────────────────────────────────\n  16.3 protein subunits per helical turn\n  2040 identical coat protein subunits total\n  ssRNA 6.4 kb: lies in a groove on the inner surface of the helix\n  Diameter: 18 nm, Length: 300 nm (proportional to genome)\n  Self-assembles from denatured state in vitro (first virus assembled in test tube)"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#015",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "INFLUENZA NUCLEOCAPSID:\n  ─────────────────────────\n  8 genome segments, each independently helical (ribonucleoprotein, RNP)\n  NP protein coats each RNA segment\n  Surrounded by matrix protein M1, then lipid envelope\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#016",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
