        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### Complex Capsids"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#017",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  BACTERIOPHAGE T4:\n  ──────────────────\n  Prolate icosahedral head (elongated) + tail assembly\n  Head: 166 nm × 111 nm, T=13 hexagonal grid on head body\n  Tail: central tube (DNA injection), contractile sheath, tail fibers (recognition)\n  Baseplate: activated upon attachment → tail sheath contracts → DNA injected"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#018",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This is basically a molecular syringe — mechanical engineering at 10 nm scale.\n  Bridge: Phage T4 injection mechanism is a nanomachine more sophisticated than\n  anything human nanotechnology has yet built."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#019",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
