        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "POXVIRUSES (e.g., smallpox, vaccinia):\n  ─────────────────────────────────────\n  Brick-shaped, ~200-300 nm × 250-350 nm\n  Not classically icosahedral or helical\n  Contain their own transcription machinery (unusual: most DNA viruses use host)\n  Two forms: intracellular mature virion (IMV) and extracellular enveloped virion (EEV)\n```"
    },
