      "text": "## The Lipid Envelope"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#022",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Enveloped viruses acquire a membrane during budding from the host cell (or nuclear\nmembrane). The envelope lipid composition reflects the host membrane but is enriched\nin the viral glycoproteins."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#023",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  ENVELOPED VIRUS CROSS-SECTION:\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Surface glycoproteins  ←─── gp120/gp41 (HIV), HA/NA (flu),\n  (projecting outward)          S protein (SARS-CoV-2)\n         │\n  ───────┼─────────────────────────────── lipid bilayer\n         │         ↑ host-derived membrane\n  Matrix protein (inside face of envelope; M protein in flu)\n         │\n  Capsid/nucleocapsid (innermost)\n  └─ Genome inside\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#024",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "KEY SURFACE PROTEINS (by virus):\n  ──────────────────────────────────\n  HIV:           gp120 (CD4/CCR5 binding), gp41 (membrane fusion)\n  Influenza:     HA (hemagglutinin; sialic acid binding + fusion)\n                 NA (neuraminidase; cleaves sialic acid → release)\n  SARS-CoV-2:    S (spike; ACE2 binding + furin cleavage + fusion)\n  Ebola:         GP (glycoprotein; NPC1 receptor in late endosome)\n  Herpesvirus:   gB + gH-gL complex (core fusion machinery)\n```"
    },
