      "text": "### Genome Size and Information Density"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#030",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  VIRUS SIZE SPECTRUM:\n  ─────────────────────\n  Circovirus (porcine):  1.7 kb,  2 ORFs       Smallest known\n  Poliovirus:            7.5 kb,  1 polyprotein\n  HIV:                   9.7 kb,  9 genes\n  Influenza A:           13.6 kb, 8 segments, 10-14 proteins\n  Herpes simplex 1:     152 kb,  74 ORFs\n  Megavirus chilensis:   1.26 Mb, >1000 ORFs\n  Pandoravirus salinus:  2.47 Mb, ~2,500 ORFs"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#031",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "OVERLAPPING READING FRAMES:\n  ─────────────────────────────\n  RNA viruses especially compact: multiple ORFs may overlap\n  HIV: 9.7 kb genome encodes 15 proteins via:\n  - Alternative splicing\n  - Frameshift signals (ribosomal frameshifting)\n  - Regulatory/non-structural proteins with multiple functions"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md#032",
      "path": [
        "01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:virology:01-virus-structure, git-history:virology:01-virus-structure]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "current_path": "virology/01-VIRUS-STRUCTURE.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:virus-structure",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[virus, structure]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virus Structure and Genome Organization",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Bridge: viral genome compactness is a constraint-satisfaction problem.\n  Given limited genome space, encoding more proteins requires overlapping\n  frames, polyprotein processing (one ORF → many proteins via protease),\n  and read-through strategies. RNA viruses are the most information-dense\n  coding sequences known.\n```"
    }
